From: Joshua Bryan <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:25:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] feat(plugin-mcp): read-version precondition for update
 and delete by id

C-readversion: the version each user last read (find, create, update) is the precondition for an
update or delete by id that carries no ifUpdatedAt; a document changed by someone else since is refused as
a stale Conflict with the current updatedAt and a re-read-and-retry instruction. In-process memory keyed by
user, collection, id and createdAt; best-effort (read then write, not atomic).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
